advisor-ts orchestrates the spore.host browser-native libraries (truffle-ts,
lagotto-ts, spawn-ts) as tools callable by a large language model hosted in the
user's own AWS account via Amazon Bedrock.

Every hardware fact in an answer — instance type, price, quota, capacity — comes
from a tool call and is cited. Workload characterisations may come from the
model's own knowledge and are labelled as inference, never as retrieved fact.
The seed workload knowledge base (src/core/workloads.ts) carries a provenance
citation per entry and is deliberately small: it overrides model inference only
where a verified opinion exists.

Amazon Bedrock inference is billable. Nothing in this library calls Bedrock
unless a caller explicitly constructs a Bedrock client and invokes it; no test
in this repository performs live inference.
